    open or closed, with no notice to keep. Full text in LICENSES/MIT-0.txt.

Games made with Rocinante belong to their authors. Rocinante claims nothing
over a game's texts, pictures or logic.

Unless stated otherwise, every file in this repository is under the AGPL.
The following are under MIT-0, because they end up inside exported games
(each one says so in its first line, except page.html and screen.css,
which are copied as they are into every exported web page):

  src/player/              the web player of exported games (main.js, run.js,
                           page.html, screen.css)
  src/daad/engine.js       the DAAD engine in JavaScript
  src/daad/condacts.js     the condact table it uses
  src/spectrum/daadscreen.js, src/spectrum/screen-io.js
                           the Spectrum text screen
  src/web/view.js, src/web/web-io.js
                           the screen and keyboard in the browser
  src/gfx/drawstring.js    vector pictures
  z80/                     the Z80 routines: memory banks and pictures
                           (xbank), tape loader (tapload) and MSX cartridge
                           start-up (msxcart, msxmover, msxhooks), and the
                           files assembled from them: src/daad/xbank-bin.js,
                           src/spectrum/tapload-bin.js, src/msx/msxload-bin.js

Besides those files, MIT-0 also covers every other piece of Rocinante as it
appears in a saved project or an exported game: the contents of the new-game
templates (vocabulary, system messages, processes), the loaders, BASIC
lines, boot blocks and configuration files the exporters write (for example
the Amiga boot block and Startup-Sequence, the Atari ST DESKTOP.INF, the PC
batch file and its instructions), and the changes Rocinante makes to the
character sets.

If you modify the editor and let other people use it over a network, the
AGPL asks you to offer them the source code of your version (section 13).

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT
ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licence texts for details.

