Third-party material

The Spectrum snapshots that Rocinante exports embed the DAAD interpreters for
the ZX Spectrum (DS48IS, Spanish version, and DS48IE, English version) by
Infinite Imaginations / Aventuras AD, which were released into the public
domain, together with the PART1.SDG character set from the same release. They
are stored in src/spectrum/daadbase.js, src/spectrum/charset-default.js and
ref/. They are not covered by Rocinante's licences.

In the same way, the Amstrad CPC exports embed the public domain DAAD
interpreters for the CPC (DCPCIS, Spanish, and DCPCIE, English) and the
character set of their empty graphics database (GFX.BIN), taken from
github.com/daad-adventure-writer/DAAD. They are stored in src/cpc/cpcbase.js
and ref/cpc/. They are not covered by Rocinante's licences either.

The Commodore 64 exports embed, likewise, the public domain DAAD loader
(boot.prg), the C64 interpreters (SDI64, Spanish, and EDI64, English) and the
character set of their graphics database (apart1.prg), from the same
repository. They are stored in src/c64/c64base.js and ref/c64/ and are not
covered by Rocinante's licences.

The MSX exports embed the public domain DAAD interpreters for the MSX
(MSXSDI.Z80, Spanish, and MSXEDI.Z80, English), from the same repository,
started by Rocinante's own cartridge loader (z80/msxcart.asm, MIT-0). They are
stored in src/msx/msxbase.js and ref/msx/ and are not covered by Rocinante's
licences.

The PC exports embed the public domain DAAD interpreters for MS-DOS
(INTSM1.EXE, Spanish, and INTEM1.EXE, English), from the same repository.
They are stored in src/dos/dosbase.js and ref/dos/ and are not covered by
Rocinante's licences.

The Atari ST and Amiga exports embed the public domain DAAD interpreters for
those machines (SDI1.PRG and EDI1.PRG for the ST, sdi1 and edi1 for the
Amiga, Spanish and English) and the 128-byte header of their character set
file (PART1.CHR), from the same repository. They are stored in
src/m68k/m68kbase.js, ref/atari/ and ref/amiga/ and are not covered by
Rocinante's licences.

No ROM of any machine is included. The emulator tests download the Amstrad
ROMs (tools/setup-cpc.sh), the Commodore ROMs (tools/setup-c64.sh) and
EmuTOS (tools/setup-atari.sh, GPL) separately; the MSX test uses C-BIOS
(free software, installed with the emulator). The Amiga test needs a
Kickstart 1.3 ROM that each developer must supply.

test/blank_es.dsf and test/blank_en.dsf are the DAAD blank database templates
(based on the original BLANK.SCE by Tim Gilberts and Andrés Samudio), as
distributed with DRC. They are only used as input to build test cases.

Preact (MIT, copyright Jason Miller) is bundled into the editor,
dist/rocinante.html, which carries its notice; the full text is in
LICENSES/Preact-MIT.txt. It is not part of exported games.

No code from DRC/DRB (GPL) is included. DRC was only used locally to build
test databases during development.
